# React components — small and reusable

Agents often dump a whole page (markup, state, handlers, fetch) into one `.tsx`. Do not.

## Rules

- **Pages/routes orchestrate** (data, layout slots). They must not contain large inline UI trees.
- Extract a component when a block has its own markup + state/handlers, or when the same UI will be reused.
- Prefer reusable components over copy-paste JSX.
  - Shared (2+ features) → `components/` (or `src/components/` for Vite/SPA)
  - Feature-only → follow the stack structure rule (`app/<feature>/_components/` or `src/pages/<Feature>/components/`)
- Soft limit: if a `.tsx` grows past **~150 lines**, split before adding more. Real UI units — not one-line wrappers (YAGNI).
- One component, one job. Pass props instead of duplicating JSX.
- Naming: `PascalCase.tsx` for components; hooks `useThing.ts`; avoid `Component2`, `Helper`, `Utils.tsx`.

```tsx
// BAD — everything in page.tsx (fetch + table + modal + filters inline)

// GOOD — page composes pieces
export default function UsersPage() {
  return (
    <>
      <UsersFilters />
      <UsersTable />
      <UserEditModal />
    </>
  );
}
```
